    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="d162-03" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve06/d162-03"/>

                <head>163. Memorandum From the Executive Secretary of the Department of State
                        (Borg) to the President’s Assistant for
                    National Security Affairs (Scowcroft)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d163-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d163-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1976-08-13">August 13, 1976</date>
                </dateline>
                <pb facs="d163-01" n="1" xml:id="d163-01"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Follow-up on Ad Hoc Interdepartmental Group’s Study in Response NSSM 239: The Future of the French Territory
                        of the Afars and the Issas (FTAI)</item>
                </list>
                <p>In view of the recent changes in the situation with regard to the FTAI (e.g.
                    election of new government, advance of referendum to January, 1977) the ad hoc
                    interdepartmental Group is submitting herewith an updating of the situation. We
                    will shortly be sending our formal agency comments on the study on the future of
                    the FTAI prepared in response to NSSM 239.</p>
                <closer><signed>Peter Bridges for<lb/>C. Arthur Borg</signed>
                    <affiliation>Executive Secretary</affiliation></closer>


                <xi:include href="d163-a1.xml" xpointer="d163-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d163-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d163-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Ford Library, National Security
                    Adviser, NSC Institutional File, Box 46, IF/NS
                    File for the President, NSSM 239. Secret;
                    Noforn</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d163-f2" n="2" xml:id="d163-f2-content">
                <p>The memorandum forwarded a follow-up study on the response to NSSM 239 owing to recent changes in French
                    Territory of the Afars and the Issas (FTAI), including election of a new
                    government and advancing a referendum to January 1977.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
